{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/533700-would-altered-carbon-style-resleeving-work-in-trinity","id":533700,"title":"Would \"Altered Carbon\" style resleeving work in Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-30T15:47:47-07:00","id":533700,"title":"Would \"Altered Carbon\" style resleeving work in Trinity","content":"Just an idea, but I was wondering if anyone has thought about having resleeving (as in the book &quot;Altered Carbon&quot; or in games like Eclipse Phase) work in the Trinity setting? Perhaps as something only the Japanese cyborgs could do? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5930-deathchipmunk","name":"DeathChipmunk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:16:05-07:00","id":533748,"title":"","content":"It could, certainly. I've run a setting hack where the players' characters could switch organic and mechanical bodies - different bodies have different physical Attributes and other abilities while the PC keeps the same mental Attributes and learned abilities. I statted out the variant bodies along with the players, keeping them near human power levels, and introduced some related drawbacks such as delays in actions caused by interference, so they weren't unbalanced against non-sleeved characters.<br /> <br /> One thing to work out in the <b>Trinity</b> future specifically would be whether or not Psionic abilities transfer, as it's the same 'mind' in a different physical brain. Perhaps it only works with cloned copies of the psions' own brains, so the most powerful mechanical bodies cannot use it and the cloned brains are harder to replace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T22:40:09-07:00","id":534048,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the boards, DeathChipmunk.<br /> I've not heard of Eclipse Phase, so &quot;resleeving&quot; and &quot;Altered Carbon&quot; are just jingo - but post/transhumanism is one of the elements hinted at but never detailed in Trinity. Another poster here reminded me this is likely because of the Aberrant war's early disasters in the science. I loved &quot;Transhuman Space&quot; and the hardware approach to physical bodies, so i would probably use the idea regardless of whether rules were presented to accomodate it.<br /> I used an 'uploaded' machine intelligence as a recurring villain and intimated other cybernetic solutions, but i failed to really do justice to biological variants on the solution. Bue Li is doing some pretty spectacular post-human stunts in Asia Ascendant as is Del Feugo in Terra Verde - this stuff is already kind of there, it just never got the spotlight it deserves.<br /> <br /> Good post, Mr. Oxbrow, Noetic nesting of Psionic/Quantum/Daredevil inspiration would have to be adressed in any system opened to players. I personally liked to use post-humans as a leveling tool against tainted nova PCs, so i was less concerned with balancing against Psion PCs - which lead to some grand trans-humanist constructs that would likely smear many parties of psions relentlessly.<br /> I would assume that only Noetically engineered biotech of sufficient elegance could possibly transfer the biological foundations for Psi/Quantum/Inspiration into an alternate shell - maybe systems capable of this are still in testing in 2120, but Noetically blind post-human systems have been available (at least on the black-market) for decades in some cases.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:07:58-07:00","id":534212,"title":"","content":"Eclipse Phase is a post-apocalyptic pseudo-hard transhuman sci-fi/horror game where you mind (or Ego) is essentially a program running on the hardware of your body (or Morph). You can adjust your Ego, copy it, load it into multiple Morphs and so on. Morphs are by no means limited to biological bodies, either. In the setting a large amount of transhumans in places like Mars and Lunar are loaded into synthetic Morphs or indeed have no body at all, existing entirely as a mesh entity stored on a Server somewhere. Other morphs include animal based morphs, half biological and half synthetic morphs and so on. A starting character can just as easily be a giant (six foot tall) crab made for vacuum and zero-g operations as they can be what we would call humans.<br /> <br /> If you die, in EP, it's likely that your Morph died. Your Ego can be recovered from your Morph's stack, which is a tiny little computer that stores the Ego, and can be then loaded (or Sleeved) into another Morph. If the stack is lost, then you can be restored from back-up (or Re-sleeved)<br /> <br /> It's a very cool game. I'd introduce some transhuman elements to Trinity myself, though a lot of the questions posed by the transhuman tech in EP (when you switch bodies, do you essentially die while another you continues to live?) are deliberately unanswered to try and make the setting deliberately unsettling and creepy. Trinity doesn't seem to really draw upon existential horror tropes in the same way, so rather than giving a hard answer to those queries I'd probably make transhuman technology more based around the modification of your own body and such, with re-sleeving, personality programming and so on being something that is either theoretical or only exists in the most top end of secret research labs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:42:35-07:00","id":534232,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree that Trinity doesn't do existential horror, but i may have taken an unusual path in my games. Otherwise, i would assume that really elegant nesting of consciousness might still be a few years down the track from Trinity, mostly because of the political resistance to post-human development in the shadow of the Aberrant war.<br /> An avenue primed for the super-science of 2120+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:50:16-07:00","id":534235,"title":"","content":"Well, I think it's fair to say that it can do existential horror, but doesn't <i>typically</i> do so. EP is all about existential horror, so there is a different objective for the game there. And yes, I think it's very much got a place as the cutting edge tech in Trinity, the tech that characters need to recover from illegal black site labs they've shut down and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:27:24-07:00","id":534481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/533700-would-altered-carbon-style-resleeving-work-in-trinity?p=534232#post534232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree that Trinity doesn't do existential horror, but i may have taken an unusual path in my games. Otherwise, i would assume that really elegant nesting of consciousness might still be a few years down the track from Trinity, mostly because of the political resistance to post-human development in the shadow of the Aberrant war.<br /> An avenue primed for the super-science of 2120+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something in the edge of known space, half fact, half spacer legend, somewhat like Xenomorphs, maybe... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}